# Copy to .env — never commit the real one.
#
# ticker-news-signals needs NO API keys for its core path: GNews and the RSS
# provider are keyless, and sentiment scoring is local (VADER / lexicon).
# Everything below is optional tuning; unset values use built-in defaults.

# ── Source selection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated provider names: gnews, rss, bingnews, cryptopanic.
# Unset = use every provider that is available.
# TNS_SOURCES=gnews,rss,bingnews

# Optional CryptoPanic token — a free auth token lights the provider up.
# Without it CryptoPanic is skipped (with a recorded reason).
# TNS_CRYPTOPANIC_TOKEN=your-token

# RSS feeds for the rss provider: name=url, comma-separated.
# Unset = a curated keyless default set (CoinDesk, Cointelegraph, Decrypt,
# BeInCrypto, NewsBTC, Bitcoinist, U.Today, ZyCrypto, …).
# TNS_RSS_FEEDS=coindesk=https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/

# Bing News (bingnews) is keyless and per-ticker queryable; no setting needed.
# It shares the TNS_RATE_LIMIT safety net with the other sources.

# ── Sentiment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend: vader (default), lexicon (crypto-domain), ensemble (mean of the
# independent scorers, with per-headline disagreement surfaced as scorer_std).
# cryptobert becomes available after `pip install -e ".[ml]"`.
# TNS_SENTIMENT=vader

# ── Query shaping ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Language / region of the Google News feed (Falls back to TICKER_NEWS_*).
# TNS_LANGUAGE=en
# TNS_COUNTRY=US
# How far back the GNews feed reaches (h/d/m/y).  The pipeline sizes this
# from --lookback-hours automatically; override to change the feed window.
# TNS_PERIOD=1d
# Per-source result ceiling.
# TNS_MAX_RESULTS=100
# Default aggregation window, hours.
# TNS_LOOKBACK_HOURS=1
# Age within which a headline marks its hour as novel.
# TNS_NOVELTY_MINUTES=15

# ── Reliability ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-source requests-per-minute safety net.
# TNS_RATE_LIMIT=60
# Per-request timeout, seconds.
# TNS_TIMEOUT=15
# Retry policy for 429/5xx/timeouts (jittered exponential backoff).
# TNS_MAX_RETRIES=3
# TNS_RETRY_BASE_DELAY=0.5
# TNS_RETRY_MAX_DELAY=8.0
# Longest server-parked wait honoured via Retry-After.
# TNS_MAX_RETRY_AFTER=60

# ── Cache ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set TNS_CACHE_PATH to persist responses to a git-trackable SQLite file
# (bounded, LRU-evicted; `ticker-news-signals cache stats` to inspect).
# TNS_CACHE_PATH=ticker_news_signals_cache.sqlite3
# TNS_CACHE_TTL=300
# TNS_CACHE_ENABLED=1
# TNS_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES=2000
# TNS_CACHE_MAX_BYTES=10485760